1. Added Suspense wrapper to handle any lazy-loaded components
2. Added mock providers that match the component stack trace
3. Moved the global mocks into a useEffect to ensure they're only set once after component mount
4. Improved the mock components with better structure and error handling
5. Added proper TypeScript types for the mock components
6. Wrapped the ImportedComponent with all necessary providers in the correct order based on the stack trace

The error was likely occurring because:
1. The component was trying to access providers that weren't available in the preview environment
2. The dynamic import was failing due to missing context providers
3. Global mocks weren't properly initialized

The changes should resolve the "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module" error by providing the necessary context and mocks for the component to render properly.

